importer.ai_prompt:
Generate only a valid JSON object to import a threat model into Tamandua. Use this example as the contract and adapt the names, components, flows, boundaries and content to the system I describe. Keep format="tamandua-threat-model", version=1 and the given methodology. IDs must be unique and use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens; source and target must refer to existing components; each boundary may only contain existing components. Don't include installation IDs or scan evidence. If you mention repositories or domains, use repository_refs or asset_ref: they will stay pending until someone links them. Don't add sections from another methodology; to combine them, use methodology="custom" and enable them in custom_modules. Don't include position, size or box: Tamandua lays out the diagram from the boundaries and flows. Available kinds: actor, web_app, api, service, function, database, cache, queue, storage, external, identity; for anything else, use kind="custom" with custom_kind (its name) and custom_base (one of the kinds above, the role it is analyzed as). Return only JSON, without Markdown.

Example:
{{example}}
